title: has_id reports a notification as having an id - the predicate only checks existence
updated: 2026-10-20T04:53:24Z
---

`lib/WWW/MailboxOrg/JSONRPCRequest.pm`:

    has id => (
        is       => 'ro',
        predicate => 'has_id',
    );

The predicate that Moo generates here is exists-based (`exists $self->{id}`), and the builder passes `id => undef` explicitly, so the key exists even when the value is undefined. A notification therefore answers `has_id` with true, although it has no id.

`t/00-load.t` and `t/01-http.t` check `has_id` only for a request that really has an id, so the wrong answer is not covered.

Done when: the predicate answers "has an id" for a request and "has no id" for a notification, and a test covers both. The same predicate exists on `JSONRPCResponse` (line 46) - check whether it needs the same treatment.

